I'll review the jsonl port read-only against the pinned upstream oracle, the round-2 inventory, and the binding port decisions. First I'll load those constraints and the module surface so I don't reopen closed items.Round-2 left four required defects. I'll check those fixes on this commit, then compare the port to the pinned oracle for anything the gates would not catch.The patch encoder drops the class prototype that used to pick a union member. I'll probe a two-class union against the lab and the pinned oracle.The union-encode trace is the open required item. I am re-reading the patch path, the merge, and the oracle so the finding cites this commit’s lines.### fable-3-1
- file: scratchpad/effected/jsonl/Envelope.ts:290
- class: bug   severity: required
- standard: D9, D11; section 14. The native-runtime ledger row (`PORT_LEDGER.json` jsonl deviations, test pin `Journal.test.ts:278`) says the plain merge is lawful only because `encodePatchResult` encodes that member's fields and the original codec then builds the instance. Round-2 `sol-2-1` already ruled that this representation change does not authorize a further regression. Do not restore `Object.create`.
- evidence: `appendPatch` merges with `shallowMerge` (`Journal.ts:1128`, `internal/merge.ts:149`), a plain spread. `R.keys` does not copy the prototype getter `~effect/Schema/Class/${identifier}` (`Schema.ts:15971–15989`). `patchAst` then treats every class declaration as satisfied by any record-like value (`Envelope.ts:290`). Encode flips that declaration in front of the struct (`SchemaAST.ts` `flip` / `Declaration.flip` at 838) and a default union keeps the first success (`SchemaAST.ts` `parseUnion` at 3925–3934). The oracle merge (`packages/jsonl/src/internal/merge.ts:109`) is `Object.create(Object.getPrototypeOf(base))`, so only the decoded member passes `instanceof`. `S.NullOr(Boxed)` and the `decodeTo(S.instanceOf(Boxed))` tests stay green because only one member accepts a record. A non-discriminated pair does not. `S.Union([AsNumber, AsString])` with `AsNumber.n: S.Finite` and `AsString.n: S.FiniteFromString` (encode is number to string, `Schema.ts:10258`), plus `extra: S.String` only on `AsString`: seed `{"n":"1","keep":"a","extra":"z"}` decodes as `AsString` on both sides. `appendPatch({ n: 2 })` then persists `{"n":2,"keep":"a"}` in the lab (`AsNumber` encodes first and `onExcessProperty` defaults to `"ignore"`, `SchemaAST.ts:490`). The pre-write `decodeResult` (`Journal.ts:835`) therefore returns `AsNumber`. Upstream persists `"n":"2"` and `"extra":"z"` and returns `AsString`. The same union with `AsString` first stays on the string encoder, so member order hides it. One shared literal sentinel still selects a single member (`SchemaAST.ts:3554`) and is not this failure.
- failure: A partial patch of a non-discriminated class union rewrites the journal line with the wrong member's encoder and drops fields that member does not own. The appended envelope is an instance of that earlier member.
- fix: On the plain merge, copy each `~effect/Schema/Class/${identifier}` marker from the base prototype chain onto the record as an own string (a `Reflect.getPrototypeOf` walk, which `canMerge` already uses). In the patched `encodingRun`, pass a record through only when it has this declaration's marker; otherwise call `ast.encodingRun ?? ast.run`. The struct encoder strips the marker before JSON. Add a `Journal.test.ts` case for `S.Union([AsNumber, AsString])` seeded with `"n":"1"` and `extra`, patched with `{ n: 2 }`, asserting the second line has `"n":"2"` and `"extra"` and `instanceof AsString`.

### fable-3-2
- file: scratchpad/effected/jsonl/Envelope.ts:295
- class: bug   severity: required
- standard: D9, D11. Same native-runtime ruling as fable-3-1: the plain record still has to encode. `SchemaAST.Suspend` is the root of `S.suspend`.
- evidence: `patchAst` rebuilds unions and declaration links, then returns every other node unchanged (`Envelope.ts:295`). `S.suspend` is a `Suspend` whose parser compiles the original thunk (`SchemaAST.ts:4032–4034`), so the class instance gate is never replaced. A payload registered as `S.suspend(() => Boxed)`, or a suspended union, therefore still requires an instance. The merged plain record fails that gate. Upstream's prototype object passes `instanceof`, and `appendPatch` writes the line. A class used directly, with `S.suspend` only on a nested field, still hits the declaration branch at the root; this is only a root `Suspend`.
- failure: `appendPatch` of a suspended class payload fails `InvalidData` and writes nothing. Upstream appends the merged fields and decodes the original class.
- fix: When `SchemaAST.isSuspend(ast)`, return `new SchemaAST.Suspend(() => patchAst(ast.thunk()), ast.annotations, undefined, encoding, ast.context)`. Cover `data: S.suspend(() => Boxed)` beside the nullable-class test: `{ round: 2 }` keeps `phase`, returns `instanceof Boxed`, and leaves an invalid patch unwritten.

REQUIRED: 2
BACKLOG: 0
